# Annapurna Tiffins story: a kitchen that started with 6 tiffins

Savita Joshi began in 2019 cooking for six neighbours in Baner. Today we send 240 tiffins a day — still the same recipes, still the same care.

Cold-pressed groundnut oil, no ajinomoto, menu posted daily on WhatsApp.

**[Start a weekly plan](https://wa.me/919876543210)**

## How it began

Savita Joshi cooked for her family every day. Neighbours asked if she could pack a few extra tiffins. Six became twelve. Twelve became fifty. The kitchen moved to a dedicated space in Baner, but the cooking did not change — cold-pressed groundnut oil, no ajinomoto, fresh rotis every morning.

## What we believe

Food should taste like home. Not like a restaurant. Not like a factory. That means simple ingredients, daily menu changes, and portions that satisfy without stuffing you.

We deliver to Baner, Aundh, Balewadi and Pashan between 12 and 1 pm. The menu goes out on WhatsApp at 9 pm the night before. You always know what you are eating.

## Where we are today

- **2019** Year started
- **6** First customers
- **240** Tiffins sent daily
- **4** Areas we serve

## Meet Savita

Savita still oversees every batch. She tastes each sabzi and dal before it leaves the kitchen. If it is not right, it does not go out. That is the only standard we have.

## Taste the difference home-style makes

Start a weekly plan on WhatsApp. First lunch can be tomorrow.

**[Start a weekly plan](https://wa.me/919876543210)**
